{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he struck the Egyptian.</b> He found in him an offense carrying the death penalty under the laws of the children of Noah, for he was forcing himself upon this man's wife, as it is written: 'and he shall cling to his wife' — and not to another's wife — and no warning was required, as we derive from the verse: 'he shall die for the woman,' etc." "<b>And he hid him in the sand.</b> That was there for construction needs."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:49.143524285Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}